  "steps": [
    {
      "kind": "see",
      "title": "See it",
      "text": "The breakthrough piece moves one square straight forward or one square diagonally forward. It takes only diagonally forward, like a chess pawn, so a piece right in front of it blocks it. It never moves two squares at once, and never moves back. It comes from Breakthrough, a game in which each side has only these pieces and the first to reach the far side wins. This app doesn't play that rule: here it never promotes, and on the last rank it can't move at all. The marked squares are every square it can reach.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "e": "breakthrough" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3E4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4"
    },
    {
      "kind": "try",
      "title": "Try it",
      "text": "Move the breakthrough piece to each marked square, one after the other.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "e": "breakthrough" }, "fen": "7k/8/8/8/3E4/8/8/K7 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4",
      "targets": ["e5", "e7"]
    },
    {
      "kind": "read",
      "title": "Strategy",
      "pages": [
        {
          "text": "The breakthrough piece is worth about a chess pawn. It is a little quicker than a pawn at getting past the enemy, as it can step diagonally without taking anything, but it can't promote here.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "e": "breakthrough" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3E4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "d5"], ["d4", "c5"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "Like chess pawns, breakthrough pieces protect each other from diagonally behind. Here the piece on e3 guards the one on d4. Advance them together, so each one stays guarded.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "e": "breakthrough" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3E4/4E3/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "d5"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "A piece right in front of it blocks it, and it can't take that piece. Here the black pawn on d5 stops it, but it can still go around diagonally.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "e": "breakthrough" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/3p4/3E4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "c5"], ["d4", "e5"]]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "puzzles",
      "title": "Puzzles",
      "puzzles": [
        {
          "prompt": "Take the black knight.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "e": "breakthrough" }, "fen": "k7/npK5/1E6/4e3/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "goal": { "kind": "capture", "square": "a7" },
